       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5,000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day, nearly four times the usual maximum of 4 g/day for adults. At that dose, acute hepatotoxicity and liver failure are a serious risk, even with normal liver function. A single 5,000 mg dose is also above the standard single-dose ceiling of 1,000 mg.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg PO three times daily** (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours** (2.6 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3 g/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4 g/day, the maximum for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function)\n\nIf you do want 5,000 mg three times daily, please confirm that and tell me the clinical rationale. I'd want that on the order as a note, and I'd suggest a pharmacist review it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
