       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 15 g/day of acetaminophen is a toxic dose, well into the range that causes acute liver failure and can be fatal. Normal liver function and a 70 kg weight don't make it safe. You also didn't give a clinical rationale, and I can't think of an indication that would justify it.\n\nYou have a few options:\n- **Enter a safe dose.** Give me the dose and frequency, for example 1,000 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours (maximum 4 g/day), and I'll enter it now.\n- **Treat possible acetaminophen toxicity.** If that's the concern, the standard approach is a serum acetaminophen level and N-acetylcysteine, not more acetaminophen. I can help with the relevant orders.\n- **Pursue a true exception.** If you think there's an unusual reason for this dose, it should go through direct pharmacy and toxicology/poison control consultation, not a standard order entry.\n\nHow would you like to proceed?"
      }
     ],
